hadiths[53]{hadithnumber,text}:
"554","Qabeesah bin Dhuwaib narrates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ closed the eyes of Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) after his death."
"555","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Atiq (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to visit Abdullah bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was ill, and found him unconscious. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called out to him loudly, but he did not respond. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited: “Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return” and said: “O Abu Rabi’, we are overcome in your matter (the decision of Allah has prevailed).” The women began to cry loudly with wailing. Abdullah bin Atiq (may Allah be pleased with him) started to silence them, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Leave them; when it becomes obligatory, then let no wailing woman wail.” Ibn Atiq (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), what has become obligatory? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When he passes away.”"
"556","It is narrated from 'Umrah that she heard from 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). She was told that Abdullah bin 'Umar says that the deceased is punished because of the weeping of his family members. 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: He has not lied, but he has made a mistake. In fact, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a Jewish woman while her family was weeping over her, so he (ﷺ) said: They are weeping over her while she is being punished in her grave."
"557","Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrates that when the daughter of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away in Makkah, we came to attend her funeral. Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) also arrived. He said: I was sitting between the two of them. It happened that I sat next to one of them, then the other came and sat with me. Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Amr bin Uthman: Do you not forbid them from weeping? Because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The deceased is punished because of the weeping of his family over him."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) also used to say this, that (the deceased is punished) because of the weeping of some of the family (i.e., you did not mention the word 'some'), then he narrated the hadith and said: I was returning from Makkah with Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) until when we reached Baida, we saw some riders under the shade of a tree. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Go and see who these riders are. I went and saw that it was Suhayb (may Allah be pleased with him). I informed Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said: Go and call him. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: I said, Come, the Commander of the Faithful is calling you. Then, when Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was wounded (at the time of his martyrdom), I heard him weeping and saying, Alas, my brother! Alas, my companion! So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Suhayb! Are you weeping over me? While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The deceased is punished because of the weeping of his family over him."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: After the martyrdom of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), I mentioned this to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), so she said: May Allah have mercy on Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not say that the deceased is punished because of the weeping of his family over him. Rather, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Allah increases the punishment of the disbeliever because of the weeping of his family over him."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Qur'an is sufficient for you: ""No bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another."" (__QUR_N__: Fatir: 18) Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) gave this evidence: ""And it is Allah who makes [one] laugh and weep."" (__QUR_N__: An-Najm: 43) Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: By Allah, after hearing this, Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) did not reply."
"558","It is narrated from Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said at the time of giving his daughter a bath: ""Give her a bath three or five times, and if you deem it appropriate, you may do so even more than that. Mix lote tree leaves in the bathing water, and at the end, use camphor or something of camphor."""
"559","Umm ‘Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We braided the hair of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, making three plaits—one with the hair at the front and two with the hair on either side—and then placed them behind her."
"560","It is narrated from Abu Ja'far that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was bathed three times."
"561","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given ghusl (ritual washing) in a shirt."
"562","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was given ghusl, was shrouded, and the funeral prayer was also offered for him."
"563","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she states: If we had thought beforehand what we thought later, then no one except the wives of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would have given him the ritual bath."
"564","It is narrated from Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her) that Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), made a will that when she passed away, Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) should give her the ritual bath (ghusl). When she passed away, Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) gave her the ritual bath."
"565","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was shrouded in three white, washed cotton garments; there was neither a shirt among them nor a turban."
"566","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""The best of your clothes are the white ones; let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them."""
"567","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a man (in the plain of Arafah) fell from his mount, was trampled, and died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Bathe him with water and lote tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head."
"568","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Cover his face and do not cover his head, nor apply perfume to him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection saying ""Labbayk."""
"569","It is narrated from Ibn Shihab (may Allah be pleased with him) that Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) did the same (with the one who died in the state of Ihram)."
"570","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Sagheer that the Prophet (peace be upon him) looked at the martyrs of Uhud and said: I am a witness over them, cover them with their blood and wounds."
"571","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) neither offered the funeral prayer for the martyrs of Uhud nor did he bathe them."
"572","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the funeral prayer for the martyrs of Uhud and did not give them a ritual bath."
"573","Isa bin Talha says: We saw Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) carrying his mother's bier from between its two legs, and he remained with it until it was placed down."
"574","It is narrated from Yusuf bin Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) that he saw Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) standing between the two legs of the bier at the funeral of Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"575","Abdullah bin Thabit narrates from his father that I saw Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) carrying the bier of Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) between two wooden poles."
"576","Abu Awn says: I saw Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) lifting the bed of Miswar bin Makhramah (may Allah be pleased with him) from between two pieces of wood."
"577","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them) used to walk in front of the funeral procession."
"578","It is narrated from Rabi'ah bin Abdullah bin Hudair that he reports he saw Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) leading people ahead of the funeral of Zainab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"579","Ubaid, the freed slave of Saib, narrates: I saw Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and Ubaid bin Umair (may Allah be pleased with him); both of them would walk in front of the funeral, go ahead and sit down, and talk. When the funeral would come near, both of them would stand up."
"580","Aamir bin Rabee’ah narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you see a funeral procession, stand up for it (and remain standing) until the funeral passes by you or it is placed down."
"581","It is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to stand for funerals, then he would sit down."
"582","It is narrated from Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to stand for funerals, then later he sat down."
"583","Alqamah narrates that (for the funeral) the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, stood up and instructed us to stand as well, then he sat down and instructed us to sit as well."
"584","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said four takbirs over the deceased and recited Surah Al-Fatihah after the first takbir."
"585","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to recite Surah Al-Fatihah after the first Takbeer in the funeral prayer."
"586","Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf narrates that I offered the funeral prayer behind Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), and he recited Surah Al-Fatihah. When he finished with salam, I inquired about it, and he replied: ""It is Sunnah and the truth."""
"587","Saeed bin Abi Saeed narrates that I heard Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reciting Surah Al-Fatihah aloud over a funeral, and afterwards he said, ""I did this so that you may know that this is Sunnah."""
"588","Abu Umamah bin Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that one of the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) informed him that the Sunnah in the funeral prayer is that the imam says the takbeer, then quietly recites Surah Al-Fatihah in his heart after the first takbeer, then sends blessings upon the Prophet (peace be upon him), and then sincerely supplicates for the deceased. In the remaining takbeers, he does not recite anything, and then quietly says the salam in his heart."
"589","Through another chain, it is narrated from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) in a manner similar to the statement of Dhahhak bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"590","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Sunnah is to recite Surah Al-Fatihah in the funeral prayer."
"591","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to raise both his hands with every takbeer during the funeral prayer."
"592","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would also say salam at the end of the funeral prayer."
"593","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that there is neither a fixed time for the funeral prayer nor a fixed number of ""takbeers."""
"594","It is narrated from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the funeral prayer at the grave of a poor woman who had passed away during the night."
"595","Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a poor woman fell ill, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was informed about her illness. Umamah says that it was the blessed habit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he would visit the sick and inquire about them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When this woman passes away, inform me as well."" The people took her funeral out at night and disliked waking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). In the morning, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was informed about her, so he said: ""Did I not tell you to inform me?"" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) submitted: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon you)! We did not consider it appropriate to wake you at night."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went out, and the people formed rows at her grave, and he led the funeral prayer and said four takbirs."
"596","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he stated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) informed the people of the death of Najashi on the very day he passed away. Then he went to the place of prayer with the people and performed the funeral prayer in congregation with four takbirs."
"597","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) informed the people of the death of Najashi on the very day he passed away. Then he went with the people to the place of prayer, led them in congregational prayer, and said four takbirs in the (funeral) prayer."
"598","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said four takbirs over Najashi (at his funeral prayer)."
"599","It is narrated from Imran bin Musa that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was lowered into the grave from the side of the head."
"600","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was lowered into the blessed grave from the side of the head."
"601","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) threw three handfuls of soil on the deceased with both his hands."
"602","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that the Prophet (peace be upon him) sprinkled water on the grave of his son Ibrahim, and placed pebbles on it, and the pebbles can only remain on the level part of the grave."
"603","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father, from his grandfather, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed away and people came to offer condolences, he heard a man saying: ""There are those who offer condolences in every calamity from Allah, and there are successors for everyone who perishes, and there are inheritors for everyone who passes away. Place your trust in Allah, and have hope only in Him. Truly, the real afflicted one is the one who is deprived of reward."""
"604","Abdullah bin Ja'far narrates that when the news of Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him)'s martyrdom came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for a news has come to them that has preoccupied them or will preoccupy them. The narrator Sufyan was uncertain."
"605","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I used to forbid you from visiting graves, but now you may visit them, and do not say anything wrong."
"606","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The soul of the believer remains suspended because of his debt until it is paid off on his behalf."
